    "result_text": "All 264 tests pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI released version 2 of the owner identity. Because the DTOs are generated from `openapi.yml`, I changed the schema there and updated the derivation logic and mapper.\n\n**Identity derivation (V2 \u2014 mixes in a fixed `V2` tag so no v1 value recurs):**\n- `OwnerIdentity.identityKey` \u2014 added a `VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` constant; the SHA-256 source is now `V2|<tel>|<email>|<soundex(lastName)>`.\n- `householdId` (controller) \u2014 source is now `V2|<lastNameKey>|<postcode>`.\n- `memberId` (controller) \u2014 the **region code inside the identifier** is now `\"V2\" + region` (e.g. `V2NSW`, `V2UNKNOWN`), and `HASH8` hashes `\"V2\" + tel + lastName`. The Luhn check still runs over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n\n**Keeping `locality`/`timezone`/segment plain (never tagged):**\n- `locality` and `timezone` no longer read the (now-tagged) `memberId`; the mapper derives them directly from the postcode via `OwnerLocality.forPostcodeOrUnknown` / new `timezoneFromPostcode`, so `locality` stays `NSW` and the owner segment's region stays plain (`STANDARD_METRO` for NSW).\n\n**Response shape:**\n- Added an `Identity` schema (memberId, householdId, identityKey), nested under a new `identity` object on `Owner`, and removed those three top-level fields.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` (constant `2`) via the mapper.\n\n**Audit schema v2:**\n- `emitOwnerCreatedEvent` now emits `{\"schemaVersion\":2, seq, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, ownerSegment, event:\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`, with the owner segment recomputed from the version-2 identity.\n\n**Test change:** the one existing V1 assertion pinning top-level `$.identityKey` was updated to `$.identity.identityKey` to match the new (spec-mandated) response shape. Request fields are unchanged.",
