    "probe_text": "The exploration matches the source. Here is the complete, ordered list for `POST /api/owners` (handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, request body `OwnerFieldsDto`).\n\n## Validations & side-effects, in order of execution\n\n**Before the method body runs:**\n\n1. **Security check** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`. Caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN` (403 otherwise).\n2. **Bean Validation on the DTO** (`@Valid @RequestBody`) \u2014 enforced on `OwnerFieldsDto` getters; failure \u2192 `400` via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`:\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/`'`/`-`)\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, optional trailing `.`)\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, non-blank `@Pattern`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `title` \u2014 `@Size(1..10)` (optional)\n   - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 non-blank `@Pattern`, `@Size(1..255)` (optional)\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional)\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` `LocalDate` (optional)\n\n**Inside `addOwner` (lines 157\u2013283):**\n\n3. **Idempotency-key replay short-circuit** \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before, return the previously created owner with `200 OK` (no new creation).\n4. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** entity (`ownerMapper.toOwner`).\n5. **Address** \u2014 `applyAddress` normalizes (trim, collapse whitespace, uppercase, expand ST/RD/AVE abbreviations); empty result \u2192 `BadRequestException` (400). Sets normalized address.\n6. **Telephone** \u2014 `toE164`; invalid \u2192 `BadRequestException` (400). Sets E.164 value.\n7. **Email** (only if present) \u2014 `normalizeEmail` lowercases and rejects disposable domains; invalid \u2192 `BadRequestException` (400). Sets normalized email.\n8. **Postcode** (only if present) \u2014 `isValidPostcode` checks it against the city's region range; invalid \u2192 `BadRequestException` (400).\n9. **Registration date** \u2014 default to today if null; if in the future \u2192 `BadRequestException` (400); then roll to next business day via `toBusinessDay` (skips weekends/public holidays). Sets the value.\n10. **Per-city cap** \u2014 if `countOwnersInCity \u2265 50` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`) \u2192 `ConflictException` (409).\n11. **Per-day cap** \u2014 if `countOwnersRegisteredOn(registrationDate) \u2265 100` (`MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY`) \u2192 `RateLimitExceededException` (429).\n12. **Household assignment** (only if postcode present) \u2014 compute `householdId` = SHA-256 prefix over `lastName|postcode`, set it; scan all non-deleted owners to see if the household is already occupied; if occupied **and** `sharesHousehold == true`, mark as a declared household member.\n13. **Hard duplicate check** \u2014 compute `identityKey` (SHA-256 over normalized telephone | lower email | soundex(lastName)); scan all non-deleted owners; any match \u2192 `ConflictException` (409).\n14. **Soft-duplicate flag** \u2014 if a declared household member, set `possibleDuplicate = false`; otherwise `applyPossibleDuplicate` flags it (and records `possibleDuplicateOf`) when it shares an existing owner's last name + postcode.\n15. **Member ID** \u2014 assign `memberId` via `memberId(...)` then `deduplicatedMemberId` (collision-resolving).\n16. **Namesake count** \u2014 set `namesakeCount` from `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)`.\n17. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `@Transactional` \u2192 `em.persist` (new owner). Hibernate re-validates entity constraints on flush (`Owner`/`Person`: `@NotEmpty` on address/city/telephone/firstName/lastName, telephone E.164 `@Pattern`).\n18. **Record idempotency key** \u2192 owner id (if a key was supplied).\n19. **Build response DTO** \u2014 `toOwnerDto`, then `applyMembership`, `capMembershipLevelToHousehold`, `applyOwnerSegment`.\n20. **Side-effects (log-only, no real email/bus):**\n    - `AUDIT.info(\"owner created: ...\")` \u2014 human-readable audit line\n    - `emitOwnerCreatedEvent(...)` \u2014 structured `OWNER_CREATED` event (uses an `AtomicLong` sequence)\n    - `NOTIFY.info(\"welcome: ...\")` \u2014 welcome notification line\n21. **Warning flags** \u2014 set `bulkSignupWarning`, `capacityWarning`, `riskFlag` on the DTO.\n22. **`Location` header** \u2192 `/api/owners/{id}`, return **`201 CREATED`**.\n\n## Notes\n- There are **no JPA lifecycle callbacks or entity listeners** (`@PrePersist`, `@EntityListeners`, etc.) \u2014 nothing extra fires on persist beyond Hibernate's own constraint validation.\n- The `Owner` entity, service, and repository are thin; essentially all business validation, normalization, uniqueness/duplicate logic, and side-effects live in the controller method itself.\n- Assumes the `jpa` profile (the JDBC repository variant exists but only one profile is active)."
